Good morning! Today's release is, like v1.11.1, mostly a bug-fixer. A lot has changed behind the scenes, and it mostly has to do with...

## Editing

- **Image embedding has received a massive backend overhaul.** It should run more smoothly and take up fewer system resources from now on.

- **GIF images are now fully supported.** Animation and all. Keep in mind that they can be quite resource-heavy, as they are in most software.

- Images are now stored as *inlines* rather than *blocks*. They no longer automatically exist on their own lines, and are now flush with text.

- Deleting images from notes was broken for a time, but they can now be backspaced as normal once more.

- A known bug causing notes to autosave their contents if they were edited and then quickly closed without saving has now been fixed.


## Performance

- Display issues with existing images has been largely resolved.

- A known bug causing Sylver Ink to not completely close when exited has now been fixed.

